{
 "id": "trouble",
 "voice": "narrator",
 "text": "The ledger cannot tell her. Nor can it say which favourite is about to run out. Or which patron has bought a book every week for nine years. Or what the monsters cost. Then, one evening, the seal on the cellar door went out. Something grey and very old came up the stairs. A dust wraith. Not a pest. A dire incident. Pip, the clerk, ran to the tavern to find adventurers. A price was agreed in a doorway. Nobody wrote it down.",
